        <body>
            
            <pb xml:id="leaf001r" facs="loc_ja.00073.jpg" type="recto"/>
            
            <note type="authorial" hand="#h02" place="top">this will precede the copy sent over four days ago (the printed "personal jottings")</note>
            
            <note type="authorial" hand="#h02" place="top" rend="circled">five sheets&#8212; ABCDE</note>
            
            <note type="authorial" hand="#h02" place="top">A</note>
            
           
            <div> 
               
               <note type="work_relations" target="xxx.00588" cert="high"/>
               
               
                <delSpan seq="1" spanTo="#d001" rend="overstrike" hand="#h02"/>
                
                <head type="main">OLD ACTORS AND SINGERS</head>
                
               <head type="sub">FLITTING MENTION BY WALT WHITMAN.</head>
                
                <anchor xml:id="d001"/>
                
                
                <addSpan seq="2" spanTo="#a001" place="above" hand="#h02"/>
                
                    <head type="main" rend="tripleUnderline" xml:id="j001">Old Actors, singers, shows, &amp;c. in New York</head><metamark target="#j001" function="adjust"><add rend="circled" place="above">nonp caps</add></metamark><note type="collaborative" target="#j001" hand="#h04" place="above">brevier</note>
                
                    <head type="sub" rend="underline" xml:id="j002">Flitting mention&#8212;(with much left out.)</head><metamark target="#j002" function="adjust"><add place="left">ital)</add></metamark>
                    
                <anchor xml:id="a001"/>
                
                
                <p>S<hi rend="smallcaps">EEMS</hi> to me I ought acknowledge my debt to actors, singers <add hand="#h02" place="below"><metamark target="#a002" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h02" place="above" xml:id="a002" rend="marked">public speakers, conventions,</add> and the Stage in New York<unclear reason="illegible" resp="#sd" cert="medium">,</unclear> <add hand="#h02" place="below"><metamark target="#a003" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h02" place="left" rend="marked" xml:id="a003">my youthful days,</add> from 1835 onward<del hand="#h02" rend="overstrike" xml:id="d002">,</del><add hand="#h02" place="right"><metamark target="#d002" function="delete">&#948;</metamark></add>&#8212;say to '60 or '61&#8212;and to plays and operas generally. (Which nudges a pretty big disquisition : of course it should be all elaborated and penetrated more deeply&#8212;but I will here give only some flitting mentionings of my youth.) Seems to be now when I look back, the Italian contralto Marietta Alboni (she is living yet, <add hand="#h02" place="below"><metamark target="#a004" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h02" place="right" xml:id="a004">in Paris,<metamark target="#a004" function="add" place="below">&#8248;</metamark></add> 1891, in good condition, good voice yet, considering)with the then prominent historians Booth, Edwin Forrest, and Fanny Kemble and the Italian singer Bettini, have had the deepest and most lasting effect upon me. I should like well if Madame Alboni and the old composer Verdi, (and Bettini <add hand="#h02" place="below"><metamark target="#a005" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h02" place="left" xml:id="a005">and Brignoli,</add> the tenor<add hand="#h02" place="below"><metamark target="#a006" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add hand="#h02" place="right" xml:id="a006">s</add>, if <subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">he is</del><add place="right" seq="2" rend="marked">they are</add></subst> living) could know how much pleasure and happiness they gave me, and how deeply I always remember them and thank them to this day. For theatricals in literature and doubtless upon me personally including opera has been of course a serious factor.<add hand="#h02" place="below" rend="marked"><metamark target="#a007" function="adjust">run in</metamark><metamark target="#a007" function="add" place="below">&#8248;</metamark></add>
                
                <addSpan spanTo="#a008" xml:id="a007" rend="pasteon" hand="#h02" place="right"/>
                (The experts and <del rend="overstrike">big</del> <del rend="overstrike"><gap reason="illegible" extent="one word"/></del> musicians of my <add place="below"><metamark target="#a009" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a009">present</add> friends claim that <add place="below"><metamark target="#a010" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a010">the now</add> Wagner <del rend="overstrike">&amp;</del> and his pieces belong <add place="bwloe"><metamark target="#a011" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a011"><del rend="overstrike">far</del> far more</add> truly to me and I to them. Very likely. But I was fed and bred under the Italian dispensations, and <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">doubtless <gap reason="illegible" extent="several characters"/>'d</del><add place="above" seq="2">absorb'd</add></subst> it, and doubtless show it.)</p>
                <anchor xml:id="a008"/>
            
           
           </div>
            
            
